    name: 'Maria Gaetana Agnesi',
    born: '1718',
    died: '1799',
    place: 'Milan, Italy',
    field: 'Mathematics',
    knownFor: 'A landmark calculus textbook',
    bio: 'Agnesi wrote Instituzioni analitiche, a two-volume calculus textbook published in Milan in 1748-1749 that teaches through examples. In 1750 the Pope appointed her to the chair of mathematics at Bologna, but she never went there. After her father died in 1752 she devoted herself to charity.',
