    born: '1910',
    died: '1995',
    place: 'Chicago, USA',
    field: 'Astronomy',
    knownFor: 'The Chandrasekhar limit for stars',
    bio: 'Chandrasekhar was born in Lahore, then in British India and now in Pakistan. He joined the University of Chicago in 1937 and stayed for the rest of his life. He studied how stars are built, including white dwarfs. He shared the 1983 Nobel Prize in Physics for work on the structure and evolution of stars.',
