    knownFor: 'Bayes\' essay on probability',
    bio: 'Thomas Bayes was born around 1701, probably in London. He was a Presbyterian minister in Tunbridge Wells from the 1730s and became a Fellow of the Royal Society in 1742. His Essay towards solving a problem in the doctrine of chances was sent to the Royal Society by Richard Price after his death and printed in 1764.',
    idea: 'Start with a first estimate of how likely something is, then adjust that estimate each time you see new evidence.',
