    name: 'Bernhard Riemann',
    born: '1826',
    died: '1866',
    place: 'Göttingen, Germany',
    field: 'Mathematics',
    knownFor: 'Geometry of curved space; the Riemann hypothesis',
    bio: 'Riemann was a German mathematician at the University of Göttingen. In an 1854 lecture he described a new geometry of curved spaces, which Einstein later used for general relativity. His 1859 paper on prime numbers contains the Riemann hypothesis, still unsolved today.',
