    field: 'Mathematics',
    knownFor: 'Set theory and different sizes of infinity',
    bio: 'Cantor was born in St Petersburg, Russia, and moved to Germany at eleven. He worked at the University of Halle from 1869 and is seen as the founder of set theory, the study of collections of things. In 1874 he published a proof that the real numbers cannot be counted off in a list.',
