    knownFor: 'Early compilers and the roots of COBOL',
    bio: 'Grace Hopper was born in New York in 1906 and taught mathematics at Vassar College. From 1944 she programmed the Harvard Mark I computer. By 1952 she had an early compiler running. Her team\'s Flow-Matic language used English words and was a foundation for COBOL. She retired from the US Navy in 1986 as a rear admiral.',
    idea: 'A compiler is a program that turns instructions people can read into the code a machine runs, so people do not have to write machine code by hand.',
