    knownFor: 'Rules for zero and negative numbers',
    bio: 'Brahmagupta was an Indian mathematician and astronomer. In 628 he wrote the Brahmasphutasiddhanta at Bhillamala, now Bhinmal in Rajasthan. It gives rules for arithmetic with zero and with negative numbers. He later worked in Ujjain, a major centre of astronomy.',
