    bio: 'Noether was born in Erlangen, Germany, and earned her doctorate there in 1907. Hilbert and Klein invited her to Göttingen in 1915, but she was only allowed to lecture in her own right from 1919. Dismissed by the Nazis in 1933 because she was Jewish, she then taught at Bryn Mawr College in the USA.',
    idea: 'A symmetry is a change that leaves the laws of physics the same. Each smooth symmetry gives a conserved quantity: laws that hold at all times mean energy is conserved.',
